PREFILL GATE RESULT — 2026-09-21 (GPU window, spark1 GB10, serves fully stopped)

Re-run of the 2026-09-20 gate after the harness repair (commit 9f71b6e).
Harness: kernel_study/gemv_bench/driver_prefill.py @ 9f71b6e (rebuilt CPU-side
in a no-GPU container, GPU-run in throwaway dsv41-flash-exl3-sm121:canonical-e12
container with --gpus all, JIT inside container TORCH_EXTENSIONS_DIR=/tmp/ext,
container removed after). Protocol per PREFILL-GATE.md: --mode check first,
then --mode bench m in {64,128,256,512} --reps 5.

THE BUG (why 2026-09-20 failed 20/20): the eb78a8b G8 patch set
`gl_b_stride_k = 0` in exl3_gemm_inner_pf.cuh, believing load_b_gl fully
addresses global B. It does not — load_b_gl[i] is relative to the window base
gl_b_ptr; its k term skips blocks_n_full rows precisely because the STOCK
window base advances one k-tile per iteration (cb2/exl3_gemm_inner.cuh L168
`gl_b_ptr += gl_b_stride_k`). With the stride zeroed, shapes 2/3
(TILEBLOCKS_K=2) re-read k-tile 0 of the window on the second k-tile, and
shape 4 (TILEBLOCKS_K=1) walked all 144 k-blocks at window base +0. Hence
~100% of elements mismatched. The earlier "numpy reference check PASSED"
because that reference was derived from the same wrong window-base model (it
validated the harness against itself). FIX: G8 k-stride = TILEBLOCKS_K * 8 *
16 * bits (TILEBLOCKS_K group k-rows per k-tile); window wrap pf_b_n_off
unchanged.

PHASE A (CPU, before the window): proof_prefill_bitexact.py — stock reference
transcribed from cb2/exl3_gemm_inner.cuh L132-168 (lines asserted present at
run time), full tile-walk simulation, real pack shapes gate/up [320,144,32]
and down [144,320,32], shapes 2,3,4 (tile windows 8/16/32 n-blocks):
921,600 predicated int4 B loads, 0 mismatches, 100% trellis-word coverage per
matrix, int16 value-level spot map OK. VERDICT: BIT-EXACT.

